{"assets":["/statement-assets/f8d8b767a13e5a60a254a8883a9d9c02bfe40555be830523724dcd1166e4257c.png","/statement-assets/1a0cf0fb91799ca65b3570ba15a632afca0d88d8c3a7ce0c86b7049948fdcf41.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1926","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Vlad and Shapes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vladislav has a binary square grid of $$$n \\times n$$$ cells. A triangle or a square is drawn on the grid with symbols $$$\\texttt{1}$$$. As he is too busy being cool, he asks you to tell him which shape is drawn on the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"triangle"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a shape consisting of $$$k$$$ ($$$k \\gt 1$$$) consecutive rows, where the $$$i$$$-th row has $$$2 \\cdot i-1$$$ consecutive characters $$$\\texttt{1}$$$, and the central "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"s are located in one column. An upside down triangle is also considered a valid triangle (but not rotated by 90 degrees)."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f8d8b767a13e5a60a254a8883a9d9c02bfe40555be830523724dcd1166e4257c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two left pictures contain examples of triangles: $$$k=4$$$, $$$k=3$$$. The two right pictures don't contain triangles."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a shape consisting of $$$k$$$ ($$$k \\gt 1$$$) consecutive rows, where the $$$i$$$-th row has $$$k$$$ consecutive characters $$$\\texttt{1}$$$, which are positioned at an equal distance from the left edge of the grid."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/1a0cf0fb91799ca65b3570ba15a632afca0d88d8c3a7ce0c86b7049948fdcf41.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples of two squares: $$$k=2$$$, $$$k=4$$$."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the given grid, determine the type of shape that is drawn on it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 100$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 10$$$) — the size of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$n$$$ lines each contain $$$n$$$ characters $$$\\texttt{0}$$$ or $$$\\texttt{1}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The grid contains exactly one triangle or exactly one square that contains all the $$$\\texttt{1}$$$s in the grid. It is guaranteed that the size of the triangle or square is greater than $$$1$$$ (i.e., the shape cannot consist of exactly one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SQUARE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if all the $$$\\texttt{1}$$$s in the grid form a square, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"TRIANGLE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise (without quotes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n3\n000\n011\n011\n4\n0000\n0000\n0100\n1110\n2\n11\n11\n5\n00111\n00010\n00000\n00000\n00000\n10\n0000000000\n0000000000\n0000000000\n0000000000\n0000000000\n1111111110\n0111111100\n0011111000\n0001110000\n0000100000\n3\n111\n111\n111\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nSQUARE\nTRIANGLE\nSQUARE\nTRIANGLE\nTRIANGLE\nSQUARE\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1926B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1926/problem/B"}